        <rules>
            <name>Create_Alert</name>
            <conditionLogic>(1 OR 2) AND 3</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_Build.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Foundation_Grant</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_Build.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Government_Grant</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Already_Renewed</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Build_Task</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Create Alert</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Daily scheduled flow. Each morning it reads the configurable lead time from Grant_Renewal_Alert_Setting__mdt (Default record, Months_Before_End__c, default 6), then finds Foundation Grant / Government Grant Opportunities whose Grant End Date equals today plus that many calendar months (ADDMONTHS) and creates a renewal-alert Task owned by the Opportunity owner. Subject is &quot;Grant Renewal Alert: [Grant Name] ends in [N] months&quot; and the Task is related to the Opportunity (WhatId). Two suppressions: the alert is skipped when a renewal Opportunity already links back through Prior Cycle Grant (Renewal_Cycles), tested in bulk via a delimited-string membership check with no SOQL in the loop, and when Stage = &quot;Closed - Complete&quot; (filtered out in the query). Equality on the date means each grant fires exactly once; moving the Grant End Date reschedules it, and completing the Task dismisses it. See docs/grant-renewal-alert-task.md.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Already_Renewed</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>CONTAINS({!Renewed_Ids_CSV}, &quot;;&quot; &amp; {!Loop_Build.Id} &amp; &quot;;&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Offset_Months</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!Get_Renewal_Setting.Months_Before_End__c}), 6, {!Get_Renewal_Setting.Months_Before_End__c})</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Target_Date</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>ADDMONTHS({!$Flow.CurrentDate}, {!Offset_Months})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Task_Description</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;This grant ends on &quot; &amp; TEXT({!Loop_Build.Grant_End_Date__c}) &amp; &quot; (&quot; &amp; TEXT({!Offset_Months}) &amp; &quot; months out). Review it and start the renewal for the next cycle.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Task_Subject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Grant Renewal Alert: &quot; &amp; {!Loop_Build.Name} &amp; &quot; ends in &quot; &amp; TEXT({!Offset_Months}) &amp; &quot; months&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Create Grant Renewal Alert Task {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
